4210159420","name":"Shanghai Children's Hospital","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I4387153466","name":"Weill Cornell Medicine","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4387156387","name":"MGI","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"US","id":"I4405272987","name":"Weill Cornell Medical Center","source":"openalex_last_known"},{"country_code":"CN","id":"I4405282086","name":"Fuyao University of Science and Technology","source":"openalex_last_known"}],"rising_pct":null,"rising_score":null,"work_count":1,"work_ids":["W3203637028"]},"schema_version":"s3.1","works":[{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Animal-based studies indicate that bisphenol A (BPA) exposure is detrimental to reproductive health, but its impact on the earliest stages of germ cell development remains poorly defined. OBJECTIVES: model of early germ cell specification and differentiation, we sought to assess whether exposure to low levels of BPA prior to formation of primordial germ cells (PGCs) alters their differentiation trajectory and unique molecular program. METHODS: ) of BPA. To interrogate and characterize gene expression differences resulting from BPA exposure, we also generated RNA-seq libraries from RNA extracted from FACS-purified PGCLCs and performed transcriptome analysis using bioinformatics-based approaches. RESULTS: Exposure of EpiLCs to BPA resulted in higher numbers of cells that were associated with a higher proportion of cells in S-phase as well as a lower proportion undergoing apoptosis; this difference occurred in a concentration-dependent manner. Exposure also resulted in a greater fraction of EpiLCs showing signs of DNA damage. Remarkably, EpiLC exposure did not negatively affect PGC specification and resulted in a concentration-dependent effect on PGCLC proliferation in XX but not XY cells. PGCLC transcriptome analysis revealed an aberrant program with significant deregulation of X-linked genes and retrotransposon expression. Differential gene expression analysis also revealed the deregulation of genes associated with lipid metabolism as well as deregulated expression of genes associated with later stages of gametogenesis. CONCLUSIONS: To the best of our knowledge our findings represent the first characterization of the consequences of early BPA exposure on a model of mammalian PGC development, highlighting altered cell behavior, altered underlying pathways, and altered molecular processes. https://doi.org/10.1289/EHP8196.","author_count":4,"author_ids":["A5030182043","A5062835705","A5089759016","A5100926432"],"author_institution_ids":["I161318765"],"authors":[{"id":"A5030182043","name":"Steen K.T. Ooi"},{"id":"A5089759016","name":"Hui Jiang"},{"id":"A5100926432","name":"Yanyuan Kang"},{"id":"A5062835705","name":"Patrick Allard"}],"ca_any_author":true,"ca_led":true,"cited_by_count":13,"doi":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp8196","domain_tags":["analytical_methods","human_exposure_and_health_risk","plastic_associated_chemicals"],"facet_tags":[],"institution_ids":["I161318765"],"is_oa":true,"journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","last_updated":"2026-11-10T11:39:43.021295","license":"public-domain","needs_review":false,"oa_status":"gold","oa_url":"https://doi.org/10.1289/ehp8196","openalex_topics":["T10269","T10364","T10686"],"plastic_related":true,"plastic_tier":"chemicals-in-plastics","primary_topic":"T10686","pub_date":"2021-09-01","study_type":"article","title":"Examining the Developmental Trajectory of an in Vitro Model of Mouse Primordial Germ Cells following Exposure to Environmentally Relevant Bisphenol A Levels","type":"article","work_id":"W3203637028","year":2021}]}
